.TH JOTMAIL 1 2026-10-26 "jotmail 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jotmail \- notes from your IMAP mailbox, in a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jotmail
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B jotmail
[\fIoptions\fR] \fBlist\fR
.br
.B jotmail
[\fIoptions\fR] \fBshow\fR \fInote\fR
.br
.B jotmail
[\fIoptions\fR] \fBnew\fR [\fIfile\fR]
.br
.B jotmail
[\fIoptions\fR] \fBedit\fR \fInote\fR [\fIfile\fR]
.br
.B jotmail
[\fIoptions\fR] \fBrm\fR \fInote\fR
.br
.B jotmail
[\fIoptions\fR] \fBdump\fR \fIdir\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apple Notes, Fastmail's web Notes and ImapNotes3 keep each note as an HTML
message in a mail account's
.B Notes
folder.
.B jotmail
reads and writes that folder over IMAP, so a note edited in jotmail is seen
elsewhere as an edit, not a duplicate.
.PP
Without a command, jotmail opens a two-pane browser: the notes on the left,
the selected note on the right. Notes are edited as Markdown in
.B $VISUAL
or
.BR $EDITOR .
If a note changes on the server while it is open, the save is refused and the
text is kept in
.IR ~/.local/state/jotmail/ .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Number, date and title of every note, newest first.
.TP
.BI show " note"
Print a note's text.
.TP
.BR new " [\fIfile\fR]"
Add a note from
.IR file ,
or standard input.
.TP
.BR edit " \fInote\fR [\fIfile\fR]"
Replace a note's text from
.IR file ,
or edit it in the editor.
.TP
.BI rm " note"
Move a note to the folder marked \eTrash.
.TP
.BI dump " dir"
Save every message as \fIdir\fR/\fIuid\fR.eml, byte for byte.
.PP
.I note
is a number from
.B list
or the start of a note's UUID.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account " \fIname\fR"
An account from the configuration. The default is the configuration's
.BR default .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-folder " \fIname\fR"
Another folder than the account's. The default is
.BR Notes .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR j " " k ", arrows"
Move.
.TP
.BR enter ", " e
Edit the note.
.TP
.B n
New note.
.TP
.B p
Paste the clipboard's image into the note.
.TP
.B d d
Move the note to Trash.
.TP
.B /
Search titles and text;
.B esc
clears.
.TP
.BR J " " K ", " PgDn " " PgUp
Scroll the note.
.TP
.B r
Reload.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH IMAGES
An image in a note appears as an
.BI [attachment: id ]
line. Keep the line to keep the image; delete it to drop the image. A line
naming a file path
.RB ( / ,
.BR ~ ,
.B ./
or
.BR ../ )
attaches that PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP or HEIC file when the note is saved.
Images are drawn in kitty and Ghostty with the kitty graphics protocol,
including inside tmux with
.B allow\-passthrough
on.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/jotmail/config.toml
Accounts and settings, for example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
default = "personal"
images = "auto"          # "auto", "kitty" or "off"
mouse = true

[accounts.personal]
host = "imap.example.com"
port = 993
user = "me@example.com"
password_command = "pass show mail/me@example.com"
folder = "Notes"
# ca_file = "~/certs/my-ca.pem"

[theme]
preset = "forest"        # forest, gruvbox, nord or terminal
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B password_command
runs through
.BR /bin/sh ;
the first line of its output is the password.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/mmoyles87/jotmail
